            <ArticleTitle>Comparison of benorylate and ibuprofen in the treatment of established rheumatoid arthritis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>76-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Benorylate and ibuprofen appear to be useful drugs for pain relief in rheumatoid arthritis but benorylate would appear to have a slightly better effect on the pain score and it improved the grip strength more than the moderate doses of ibuprofen. It could be a most useful drug when gastric problems limit the dose of aspirin or of other analgesics.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
